# Dr. Denys Dutykh (Mathematics Department, Khalifa University of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi, UAE)
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as given below; the article that it accompanies is submitted."
type: software
title: "kernel-poisson: kernel Poisson regression with exposures"
abstract: >-
  Kernel Poisson and negative-binomial regression with exposures: the estimator, its Newton
  solver with Fisher-weighted landmarks, leave-one-out tuning in closed form, the competitors
  of the benchmark and the ten open data sets, with the code that rebuilds every figure and
  table of the article "Kernel Poisson Regression: Events Set the Accuracy and the Cost" by
  D. Dutykh, D. Homouz and M. Maalouf (submitted, 2026), which shows that the expected number
  of events, not the number of observations, governs the accuracy and the cost.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: LGPL-2.1-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/dutykh/kernel-poisson"
keywords:
